'''Kartak''', officially the '''Republic of Kartak''', is an island country in the [[Lesser Capuyaquiran Sea]]. It has an area of approximately 112.4 square kilometres and an estimated population of 630,201. Its capital and largest city is [[Kartak City]]. Kartak's economy is primarily oriented toward tourism and related services.

Kartak was first settled by Tapuri navigators after a vessel was driven south by a storm. It was a colony of [[Volisania]] until granted independence in 1951. Kartak is a member of the [[Adonian Community]].

== Geography ==

Kartak is a small island country in the Lesser Capuyaquiran Sea. Its area of approximately 112.4 square kilometres gives it an estimated population density of about 5,606 inhabitants per square kilometre. Most settlement and economic activity is concentrated around Kartak City and the coastal areas.

== History ==

=== Tapuri settlement ===

Kartak was likely first reached by Tapuri navigators whose vessel was driven south by a storm. The island lay approximately 140 kilometres from the nearest neighbouring island, beyond the more closely connected routes of the main Lesser Capuyaquiran settlements. The first landing was probably unplanned, but later crews returned after finding freshwater, sheltered landing sites, and productive coastal fishing grounds.

Kartak initially served as a seasonal fishing and resupply station. Tapuri crews used the island for fishing, freshwater collection, repairs, and shelter during voyages through the southern Lesser Capuyaquiran Sea. Families and boat crews later began settling permanently. Because contact with the main Tapuri communities remained intermittent, the island developed a distinct Kartaki society and dialect while retaining Tapuri ancestry, maritime practices, and elements of Tapuri material culture.

=== Volisanian rule ===

Kartak was incorporated into the Volisanian colonial system during the expansion of Volisania across the Capuyaquiran region. Its position made it useful as a southern maritime station, although it remained less politically and economically important than the larger islands. Colonial administration connected Kartak to Volisanian trade and shaped its language, legal institutions, and urban development.

=== Great Adonian War ===

During the [[Great Adonian War]], Volisania briefly occupied Kartak and used the island for air-support missions. The occupation was limited in duration and scope compared with the wartime occupation of larger Volisanian territories, but it disrupted civilian administration and tourism.

=== Independence ===

Volisania granted Kartak independence in 1951. The new republic retained close commercial and cultural connections with Volisania while developing its own political institutions. Tourism later became the principal foundation of the national economy.

== Economy ==

Tourism is the main sector of the Kartaki economy. Visitor spending supports accommodation, food services, transport, recreation, retail, and other coastal services. The small size of the domestic market makes Kartak dependent on regional trade and international visitors.

Kartak has an estimated gross domestic product per capita of I$38,432 and a Human Development Index of 0.754. The country has pursued improvements in transport, hospitality infrastructure, and public services to support tourism-oriented development.

== Demographics ==

Kartak had an estimated population of 630,201 in 2025. The population is concentrated in Kartak City and the settled coastal belt. Kartaki society reflects the island's indigenous population, Volisanian colonial history, and subsequent regional migration.

